  B.push({ h2: "7.6 Exam-day quick review" });
  B.push({ box: { kind: "ok", title: "60-second mental checklist before answering any Chapter 4 question", body: "**1)** Which of the thirteen objectives is this? Planning · communication · protocols · transactions · profiles · throughput and concurrency · script structure · script implementation · preparation · execution · reporting.  **2)** If it is a **classification** question — objective type, protocol group, audience — answer straight from the table and do not reason around it.  **3)** If it is **arithmetic**, compute **people × accesses × transactions** for the day first, then check the option's bands sum to it; and for **concurrency**, count **sessions**, never the work inside them.  **4)** If a **script misbehaves**: fails after login → **correlation**; faster on repeat → **caching**; fails on the second run → **uniqueness / parameterization**; slower than production → **locking**.  **5)** If it is about the **environment**, remember **performance is a non-linear function of the environment** and that **the load generators need monitoring too**.  **6)** If it is about **execution**, **ramp-up reaches steady state before measuring** and **spike exercises transient states**.  **7)** If it is about **reporting**, check **virtual user status first**, favour the **90th percentile**, reject **100% compliance**, and never accept a threshold the requirements did not state.  **8)** Reject any option that is **incomplete** — production testing without mitigations, risks without mitigations.  **9)** If two options survive, choose the one that repeats **syllabus wording**." } });
